A beautiful, fast, terminal-native media toolkit.

Usage: forge [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  inspect     Show duration, codecs, tracks, metadata, size, and recommended actions.
  convert     Convert media to another common format.
  compress    Shrink videos, images, or folders with sensible ffmpeg defaults.
  clip        Cut a time range or remove silence.
  resize      Resize video or images by width, height, or creator preset.
  crop        Crop to common aspect ratios such as 9:16, 1:1, or 16:9.
  captions    Attach or burn caption files.
  transcribe  Create transcripts through the local provider abstraction.
  thumbnail   Extract a still, grid, or best-frame thumbnail.
  audio       Normalize, clean, silence-trim, or extract audio.
  youtube     Wrap yt-dlp with Forgy output folders and reporting.
  batch       Run common operations across a folder.
  preset      List, show, or scaffold creator presets.
  notes       Generate local-provider-ready notes from media or transcripts.
  doctor      Check ffmpeg, ffprobe, yt-dlp, transcription, hardware, and output permissions.
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json             Print machine-readable JSON.
      --dry-run          Plan work without running media commands.
      --yes              Skip overwrite prompts and assume yes.
      --output <OUTPUT>  Output root folder. [default: forge-output]
  -h, --help             Print help
  -V, --version          Print version
